  "notes": "The _dfttrunc builds truncate the in-graph mel DFT to the bins the filterbank actually uses: bit-exact and ~1.4-2x faster on CPU/OpenVINO. Prefer them; the non-dfttrunc files are kept for existing installs. The _foldconv build folds each spectrogram's Hann window, DFT and mel filterbank into one strided Conv: not bit-exact (max logit difference 2.7e-3 against the same build without the fold over 47009 real-audio windows, no top-1 or detection changes) and about 25% faster than _dfttrunc on ONNX Runtime CPU. Do not run these fp32 files on OpenVINO ARM CPU at its default f16 precision: with a static input shape the scores collapse on low-frequency-heavy audio such as wind (see docs/birdnet-v2.4-fold-conv.md); use f32 or ONNX Runtime.",
